# mesa-gororoba install scriptlet: surface the non-obvious consequences of
# replacing system mesa with a scope-limited fork build.

_notes() {
  cat <<'EOF'
mesa-gororoba replaces stock `mesa` with an RS482-scoped fork build:
  * GL: r300 hardware + llvmpipe software fallback (egl/glx/gles/gbm/glvnd).
  * Vulkan: amd_r300 (r300vk) ICD at /usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/r300_icd.x86_64.json.
Consequences to know:
  * llvm coupling: llvmpipe links libLLVM.so of the build host's llvm major.
    If the installed llvm-libs major differs, llvmpipe paths fail to dlopen --
    rebuild mesa-gororoba against the current llvm.
  * libva-driver is provided as a no-backend virtual (RS482 has no VA-API state
    tracker); VA-API consumers install but get no hardware video decode.
  * `pacman -Syu` will conflict whenever stock mesa bumps.  Add to
    /etc/pacman.conf:  IgnorePkg = mesa-gororoba
    (or keep a local repo and rebuild on upstream bumps).
  * Rollback: pacman -U /var/cache/pacman/pkg/mesa-2:*-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst
EOF
}

post_install() {
  _notes
}

post_upgrade() {
  _notes
}
